[ I wonder if I can fit any more acronyms up there? ]

Turns out that there is more than one version of the PCI ATM NIC that
Digital sells.

One, the one I have (DGLPL-FA), is meant for NT and is NOT SUPPORTED
under Digital UNIX.

The other (DGLPB-AB), which costs roughly twice as much of course, is
theoretically supported by DU.  I call this a SUMM vs. a SUMMARY
because I haven't received the new card yet, but I trust my information
source on this one.

The moral of the story:  make sure you ask the question that I'm
surprised needs asking:  will it work with DU?

Mike

