From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Apr 16 12:12:27 1997
From: lbro () dscc ! dk
Date: Wed, 16 Apr 1997 12:12:27 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Install on LUN other than 0
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078611110453

     Hi, folks.
     
     Thanks for all the answers.
     
     
     It can be boiled down to the following:
     
     1) It is not possible to boot from LUNs other than 0, thus not
        possible to install the operating system on LUN's other than
        0.
     
     2) It should be possible to use up to 4 different SCSI adresses 
        with the HSZ40, thus making up at least 4 LUN 0 devices.
     
        -- My HSZ40 does not support that, only up to two which is
           too few having three members.
     
     3) It is altogether unsupported, says iwm@uvo.dec.com, YUCK!
     
     
     The conclution is thus:
     
     "The 'system disks' are an integrated part of the computer. If they 
     fail, the computer also fails."
     
     
     We will of course offer our customers different options like "local 
     mirror of the system disks" and "local mirror of the system disks to 
     another controller", "...to another controller and another shelf" and 
     so forth. Less elegant but a usable alternative.
     
     
     This is my conclution, comments are welcome.
     
     Lars Bro, DSC Communications Denmark
     lbro@dscc.dk

