Thanks to Dr. Tom Blinn and some jusicious reading of the release
notes for Open3D 4.2, I've made some changes to shared memory setup
using sysconfigdb.  Unfortunately, this didn't fix the problem.  I've
appended more information on the bottom:

John> We're running 4.0b (upgraded from 4.0a recently) on an AS
John> 500/400 with 384Mb of RAM, Open3D V4.2 (all subsets) and 4D60T
John> graphics installed.  We've been having a problem where the user
John> keeps getting logged out randomly from his machine and the
John> screen goes back to the login prompt.  He is using CDE as his
John> environment.  What he's doing is running some of our in house
John> codes doing simulation work and displaying graphs of the status
John> of problem as it iterates.

John> Here's the graphics info from /var/adm/mesages:

John>     Apr  9 09:15:26 lz vmunix: ingr_vga0 at pci0 slot 11
John>     Apr  9 09:15:26 lz vmunix: ingr0 at pci0 slot 12
John>     Apr  9 09:15:26 lz vmunix: ingr0:  Attached 4D60T.3.0.70.0xa FB.0.0.62.20.128.8 TP.64.0

John> When I look in /var/dt/Xerrors after he gets logged out, I see this:

John>    Adding depth 10
John>    Screen 0  Cateyes Leopard Rev-A, 1280x1024, 128 bpp, texture None, TrueColor-24
John>    shminit (255f, 48a, 0r)

John>    Fatal server error:
John>    Failed to allocate stipple bitmap


John>    Wed Apr  9 20:20:04 1997
John>    error (pid 521): Server for display :0 terminated unexpectedly 1
John>    Adding depth 10
John>    Screen 0  Cateyes Leopard Rev-A, 1280x1024, 128 bpp, texture None, TrueColor-24
John>    shminit (253f, 48a, 19r)

John> The first section and the last section are the initialization of
John> the Xserver, the middle section is the error I'm getting.  Has
John> anyone else seen this error and have a solution or a patch to
John> apply?

I've upped the default shm- variables as suggested by the release
