>When there is more than one file in the spool at the same time, the first
file is well printing but the others aren't. The spool is "emptied". Just
the first file is printing ??
>
>more precisions :
> My machine : AlphaServer 2100 OSF Unix 3.2c
> My printer :  HP-Laserjet 4MPlus 
> My /etc/printcap :
>     nab-info1|hppresn2:\
>        :lf=/usr/adm/lp4err:\
>        :lp=:\
>        :rm=nab-info1.presn2.u-nancy.fr:\
>        :rp=nab-info1:\
>        :sd=/usr/spool/lpd/nab-info1:
>
>I tried to add outputfilter, like /usr/lbin/hplaser4psof for example, to
put mx parameter but this had no effect.

FOLLOW UP :
>
>When i set banner page enabled (configuring the printer by telnet), there
is no 
>problem. What does it means ???


THE SOLUTION :

Upgrade  HP Jetdirect bios.
You can see your version by printing the AUTO-TEST. It's written in INTF MOD
table :
My REV MICROLOG was A.03.16 and now A.05.05
It works well with A.03.16 and A.04.09 but fails with A.03.06 
To do this, you have to download DLMSWIN.EXE and AMSWINE.EXE by 
        http://hpcc997.external.hp.com/cposupport/indexes1/firmwars.html
decompress the 2 files and execute the 2 setup.exe to install windows
utilities. Then, you could upgrade your printer card with "HP Download Manager".
