>I installed an isa bus modem in a DEC 2000-300 (jensen) Running DUnix
>3.2c. In the ECU, I configured it as a GENERIC OSF/1 com port, Com 3. The
>modem, of course, is configured to Com 3.
>
>When the machine boots, I get the ace1 detected message, but either there
>is no file connected to the modem in the /dev directory, or I can't find
>it. 
>

Well, I got the modem working! In fact, I  it may have been working all
along. I tested /dev/tty01 and diddnt get a response, so I assumed that
/dev/tty001 was connected to the second serial port. I  deleted /dev/tty01
and rebuilt it with the command ./MAKEDEV ace1, and I am now able to dial
the modem.

