To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: What is "module 1095:646" and "pci option table"?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078611110206


Thanks to Olle Eriksson, Dave Golden, and Dave Cherkus.
They replied so quick that I received their answers even before my question was
distributed to me!

My question:
|> at boot time I get the following message on the console:
|>    Module 1095:646 not in pci option table, can't configure it.
|> Has anyone a clue what this means?

Answer:
This is in the release notes as well as the unix manual for your
motherboard.  It is just notifying you that there is no driver
support for the on-board PCI-IDE controller.  Don't worry about it.

It means you have a pci device installed that has no Digital UNIX
device driver available.  Compare the output of the console 'show
dev' command to the unix boot strings and see if something is missing.
Also, see if the same message prints if you boot with /genvmunix.

Thanks,
   Gernot

