On Fri, 28 Feb 97 15:52:55, I wrote:
> How do I change the refresh rate on an Alpha AXP running Digital
> Unix?  Neither the graphics card nor the monitor are made by
> DEC, and it starts up with 60 Hz, though it should work with
> much more.

Thanks to:
Cliff Krieger <ckrieger@latrade.com> and
Jon Brinkmann <jb@galileo.apo.nmsu.edu> who cited
Pierre Stone <pierre@arc.arc.org.tw>,
Pete Davis <pete@eagle.deardorff.com>,
Robert L. McMillin <rlm@syseca-us.com> and
Thomas Leitner <tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at>

The solution is to edit the X startup parameters.

According to the replies, the file Xservers may be found in one
of the following directories:

/var/X11/adm/
/usr/lib/x11/xdm/
/var/X11/xdm/

You can add a -vsync parameter to /usr/bin/X11/X.

e.g.
:0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -nice -2 -screen0 1280 -vsync 72

- Willi

